  "review": {
    "summary": "I found no defects in this repair. The earlier minor issue is fixed: every 303 response now gets \"Cache-Control: no-store\" before any check that could return early. That covers null data, a bad \"now\" value, a missing Location header, an absent, null or foreign Origin, a target that fails validation, an encryption failure, and an oversized cookie value. Only non-303 responses skip the header, and they are outside this helper's purpose. The rewrite of Location to the public app address still happens only after the target, formId and path checks pass. The result cookie is still set only after encryption succeeds and the value fits the size limit. If encryption throws, the error is caught and no cookie is issued; the Location rewrite has already happened by then, but it only points to the already-checked target, so nothing is exposed. The verification function was not changed by this repair. I reviewed the supplied text only and ran no tests, so an empty findings list does not confirm that tests or the release pass.",
